{"ts": "2026-10-29T15:06:35.211607Z", "run_id": "r-20261029T1500Z-34ea", "unit": "openspec:add-api-conventions", "seq": 33, "type": "task.started", "task": "4.1", "title": "4.1 Write `test/arch/web-routes.test.ts` first (it starts with `assert.equal(typeof isReservedPath, \"function\")`; scenarios \"Reserved paths\", \"Feature paths\" over `snapshotOf` and \"API routes\"; the real-tree tests assert with `assert.ok` that `web/src/features` exists, then read `*.tsx` with `readdirSync` into a `Snapshot` of repository-relative paths and assert `checkFeaturePaths` is `[]` and that `isReservedPath(\"/\" + root.join(\"/\"))` is true for every `RESERVED_ROOTS` entry of `src/api`), then implement in `test/arch/web-routes.ts` `isReservedPath` (lower-case, cut at `?` or `#`, equal to or under `/api`, `/auth`, `/.well-known`, `/hooks`, `/callbacks`, `/mcp` or `/health`), `routesOutsideReservedRoots` (`\"<METHOD> <url>\"` per route that is not reserved, in input order, ignoring `GET /*`) and `checkFeaturePaths` (for each file of `s.files` whose path matches `^web/src/features/[0-9]{2}-[a-z0-9-]+\\.tsx$`, parse with `ts.createSourceFile(..., ts.ScriptKind.TSX)`, find the variable `feature` through `as` and `satisfies`, read the `path` property of its object literal; a string or no-substitution template literal that `isReservedPath` accepts is `ARCH_WEB_PATH_RESERVED` with the message `feature path <path> is under a reserved root: pick a web route outside /api, /auth, /.well-known, /hooks, /callbacks, /mcp and /health`; no `feature` or any other `path` is `ARCH_WEB_PATH_UNKNOWN` with the message `the path of feature must be a string literal so the reserved-root test can read it`; the line is the property's, or 1), implementing requirement \"Web pages never shadow API paths\""}
